    {
      "id": 27423,
      "name": "Spiff",
      "username": "Spiff",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-04-16T22:16:15.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>The errata says this about targets:</p>\n<p>Missing Targets</p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>No specific target: if, say, a card destroys all equipment cards in play and<br>\nthere are none actually in play, then nothing actually happens.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Specific target: However, if an attack targets the hero with the most ongoing<br>\ncards and none are in play, it is considered a tie (tied at zero) and the<br>\nplayers must choose who will receive the effect.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p>From that I would infer that a card could be legally played which required a target but for which no target actually existed.  However, there are no rules that say a card can be played directly from the hand to the discard pile without first going through being “in play”, so no discarding just because you wanted to.  These are my interpretations, at least.</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:01:23.842Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 5623,
      "topic_slug": "playing-cards-without-a-valid-target",
      "display_username": "Spiff",
      "primary_group_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_name": "playtesters",
      "flair_url": "/uploads/default/original/1X/f46928191dbf93b4d0df24571543f49779579225.png",
      "flair_bg_color": "",
      "flair_color": "",
      "flair_group_id": 41,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "The errata says this about targets:\n\nMissing Targets\n1) No specific target: if, say, a card destroys all equipment cards in play and\nthere are none actually in play, then nothing actually happens.\n\n2) Specific target: However, if an attack targets the hero with the most ongoing\ncards and none are in play, it is considered a tie (tied at zero) and the\nplayers must choose who will receive the effect.\n\nFrom that I would infer that a card could be legally played which required a target but for which no target actually existed.  However, there are no rules that say a card can be played directly from the hand to the discard pile without first going through being \"in play\", so no discarding just because you wanted to.  These are my interpretations, at least.",
